---
/**
 * Google Analytics 4.
 *
 * This is the one place on the site that measures visitors, and it is worth
 * being explicit about what it costs, because the rest of this repo is built
 * around not doing this.
 *
 * It sets cookies on arrival and sends page and event data to Google. That is a
 * real change to what this site is, and the privacy policy says so in plain
 * words rather than burying it — the previous wording ("no analytics of any
 * kind") would otherwise have become false the moment this shipped.
 *
 * Two things it deliberately does NOT change:
 *
 *   1. The extension. Nothing here is in the extension, which still sends
 *      nothing anywhere. This is the marketing site measuring the marketing
 *      site, and the product claim is untouched.
 *   2. The support messenger still loads only on a click, and scripts/qa.mjs
 *      still enforces that. Analytics loading eagerly is not a licence for
 *      every other third party to.
 *
 * CONSENT: this sends data before the visitor has agreed to anything. Most of
 * the audience is staff at international schools, so UK/EU GDPR is the relevant
 * regime and it treats analytics cookies as needing consent. Two ways to be
 * straight about that, either of which is a small change from here:
 *
 *   - Set `cookieless: true` in src/data/site.ts. GA then runs with
 *     `client_storage: "none"`, sets no cookies and stores nothing on the
 *     device. You keep pageviews and events; you lose returning-visitor and
 *     cross-session attribution.
 *   - Or keep cookies and add a consent banner, gating this behind it.
 *
 * Left as the straightforward configuration because that is what was asked for.
 * The switch is there when you want it.
 */
import { analytics } from "../data/site";
---

{
  analytics.measurementId && (
    <>
      <script
        is:inline
        async
        src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${analytics.measurementId}`}
      />
      <script
        is:inline
        set:html={`
window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
gtag('js', new Date());
gtag('config', '${analytics.measurementId}'${
          analytics.cookieless ? ", { client_storage: 'none' }" : ""
        });
`}
      />
    </>
  )
}
